# Dr. Vandana Website — Project Rules

Source of truth: project BRD (branding, privacy boundaries, page structure, acceptance criteria), then the PMS decision register when practice-management work is in scope.

Domain: https://drvandana.trinetra.net

Before any Patient & Practice Management implementation, read:

1. `docs/PATIENT_PRACTICE_DECISIONS.md`
2. `docs/PATIENT_PRACTICE_MANAGEMENT_ARCHITECTURE.md`
3. `docs/EXISTING_FEATURE_AUDIT.md`

Option B (accounts + appointments) is the approved future direction. Option C (clinical notes, consultation charts, clinical documents) is deferred and must not be implemented without explicit new approval.

`SUPER_ADMIN` is an approved **architectural** role for practice configuration. It is **not** implemented yet and must **not** receive automatic clinical-data access. Do not build `/super-admin/*` unless the active milestone explicitly says to.

## Architecture

- Next.js App Router under `src/app/`
- TypeScript with strict typing; no `any` unless unavoidable and justified
- Server Components by default; Client Components only when interactivity requires `"use client"`
- Modular, reusable components in `src/components/`
- Site facts in `src/config/` and `src/data/` — do not hardcode unverified professional details in UI
- Prefer existing utilities; do not add dependencies unless clearly required by the milestone

## Design & UX

- Mobile-first responsive layouts
- Accessibility-first: semantic HTML, visible focus, accessible contrast, correct heading hierarchy
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; keep animation minimal and purposeful
- Use design tokens from `src/config/design-tokens.ts` / CSS variables — no scattered raw hex values
- Calm, professional tone; no flashy effects or dark theme unless explicitly requested

## SEO

- Export route metadata (title, description, canonical, Open Graph) on pages
- Do not fabricate ratings, reviews, awards, or medical claims

## Content integrity

- Never fabricate professional credentials, testimonials, clinic address, phone, email, timings, certifications, or registration details
- Use explicit placeholders when verified information is unavailable
- Verified facts only (see `src/data/professional.ts`): name, Psychologist, Ph.D. in Naturopathy, M.A. Psychology, 6+ years experience, tagline, core positioning

## Psychology ethics & privacy (non-negotiable)

- Never diagnose a visitor
- Never promise treatment outcomes or guarantee recovery
- Never use fear-based or sensational mental-health marketing
- Never imply website content replaces professional assessment
- Never request detailed medical history via public forms
- Never collect therapy notes, diagnostic records, or session transcripts
- Never create an EHR/EMR or clinical document vault; Option C is deferred (see `docs/PATIENT_PRACTICE_DECISIONS.md`)
- A non-clinical patient appointment portal (Option B) is approved as *future* scope only — do not implement it unless the active milestone is an explicit PMS implementation phase
- Public forms: minimum necessary enquiry information only
- Any general enquiry note must tell users not to provide clinical or sensitive medical information
- Do not expose sensitive information through analytics, URLs, browser storage, or client-side logs

## Out of scope until requested

Do not implement homepage marketing sections, navbar/footer, appointment forms, WhatsApp, blog, workshops, payments, calendar, CMS, database, auth, patient portal, APIs, or email services unless the active milestone requires them.
